## VERDICT GRAMMAR — BINDING, READ THIS FIRST

Your report MUST end with EXACTLY ONE of these two lines, emitted UNADORNED
at column 0, on a line of its own, with no decoration whatsoever:

VERDICT: GO
VERDICT: NO-GO

NOT `**VERDICT: GO**`. NOT `(VERDICT: GO — 0 Highs)`. NOT indented, quoted or
bulleted. The only grep the driver may run is the anchored full-line
`^VERDICT: GO$`. An adorned verdict is NOT a verdict: the round is void and
must be re-run. Do not print the verdict grammar anywhere else in your report
(a prompt/spec echo containing an anchored verdict line is itself a hazard
this project has already been bitten by).

Severity tags: [H] High, [M] Medium, [L] Low. Emit NO-GO if there is any [H]
or [M]. Put your findings under a heading `## Findings`.

## WHAT THIS CHANGE IS

The M4 exit gate (`port/sim/device/verify_m4.sh`) hard-refuses to run unless
every evidence producer listed in `port/sim/device/m4-freeze-manifest.txt`
matches a reviewed pin. Each manifest record is:

    <sha256> <path> <status> <cite>

`cite` is FREE TEXT (hyphen-soup). The gate's existing stage [0] proves that
every `reviewed-go` row cites at least one `.loop/*.log` whose LAST anchored
`^VERDICT: GO$` is a GO. Three holes remained, all rooted in the cite being
prose (registered as fix_plan items C25/C26/C27):

- C25: the GO may belong to a DIFFERENT arc than the one that reviewed this
  producer. Nothing binds verdict to producer.
- C26: a GO can be positionally terminal but semantically inert (pasted
  transcript, fenced grammar example).
- C27: a non-arc row's gate claim is matched by SUBSTRING, so a cite that
  DENIES its gate (`...NOT-proven-by-SIM-CONFORMS...`) passes.

This change adds a STRUCTURED CLOSURE RECORD layer:

- `port/sim/device/m4-closure-ledger.txt` — 84 fixed-arity records, one per
  CLOSED manifest row (5 arc-in-flight rows deliberately have none).
- `port/sim/device/gen-closure-ledger.py` — derives the ledger from the
  existing corpus; refuses to write if any row cannot be derived.
- `port/sim/device/check-cite-closure.sh` — verifies it. Prints
  `CITE CLOSURE OK: ...` and exits 0; otherwise refuses and exits nonzero.
- `.loop/closure-teeth.sh` — 27 negative tests.

The checker is NOT yet wired into verify_m4.sh. Wiring is a separate,
driver-applied step (another writer owns verify_m4.sh and the manifest this
cycle, so those two files are DELIBERATELY untouched here).

## MEASUREMENTS THAT DROVE THE DESIGN (verify them; do not take them on trust)

1. 89 manifest rows: 60 reviewed-go, 20 oracle-frozen, 2 grandfathered-m1,
   2 grandfathered-m2, 5 arc-in-flight.
2. Of the 60 reviewed-go rows, 59 are GO-backed and 1 is a driver CAPPED-CLOSED.
3. Only 37 of those 59 have a terminal-GO log that literally names their own
   path; 3 more name only the basename. So the obvious rule "the cited GO log
   must name the producer" would FALSE-REJECT 22 real rows. Measured cause:
