   294	HEADER = """\
     1	# port/sim/device/m4-closure-ledger.txt — structured closure records for the
     2	# M4 freeze manifest (fix_plan C25/C26/C27). DERIVED, never hand-written:
     3	#   python3 port/sim/device/gen-closure-ledger.py --write
     4	# Verified by: bash port/sim/device/check-cite-closure.sh -> CITE CLOSURE OK
     5	#
     6	# WHY. The manifest's `cite` column is free text, so a `reviewed-go` row can
     7	# cite a real terminal GO that belongs to a DIFFERENT arc (C25), a GO that is
     8	# positionally terminal but semantically inert (C26), or, for a non-arc row,
     9	# prose that DENIES the gate it must assert (C27). Nothing in prose binds a
    10	# verdict to a producer. These records do, by identity.
    11	#
    12	# RECORD GRAMMAR — anchored, fixed arity, fail closed. Exactly 12
    13	# whitespace-separated fields; any `CLOSURE` line with a different arity is a
    14	# refusal, never a partial parse (PROCESS §3 whitelist-grammar rule):
    15	#
    16	#   CLOSURE <path> <psha> <verdict> <ev> <evsha> <vline> <cov> <covref> <covsha> <reviewer> <round>
    17	#
    18	#   path     producer path; must be a manifest row, exactly once
    19	#   psha     producer sha256; must equal the manifest row AND the bytes on disk
    20	#   verdict  GO | CAPPED-CLOSED | PROVEN-BY-HARD-RULE-3 | PROVEN-BY-M0-EXIT-GATE
    21	#            | PROVEN-BY-M1-EXIT-GATE | PROVEN-BY-M2-EXIT-GATE
    22	#            Closed vocabulary matched WHOLE-FIELD, so C27's denial hole
    23	#            ("...NOT-proven-by-SIM-CONFORMS...") is unrepresentable.
    24	#   ev       the closure log carrying the verdict (`-` when not arc-closed)
    25	#   evsha    sha256 of that log — evidence is now tamper-evident: appending a
    26	#            transcript to a cited log changes this and the gate refuses
    27	#   vline    1-based line number of the verdict INSIDE ev. The gate reads THAT
    28	#            line, requires it to be exactly `VERDICT: GO`, requires it to be
    29	#            the LAST anchored verdict in the file, and requires everything
    30	#            after it to be blank or a single reviewer RC marker (C26).
    31	#   cov      how the arc is bound to THIS producer: sha | path | base |
    32	#            ledger | gate
    33	#   covref   the artifact (or AGENT-LOG date) carrying that binding
    34	#   covsha   sha256 of covref (`-` for ledger/gate)
    35	#   reviewer codex | grok | opus5 | driver | gate  (PROCESS §4/§11 identity)
    36	#   round    the arc round; must be a substring of ev's basename
    37	#
    38	# COVERAGE IS AN ARC-LEVEL RELATION, MEASURED NOT ASSUMED. Over the live
